#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:2
msgid "How to manually configure a Git repository integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:4
msgid ""
"In this guide, you will find the steps to manually integrate your Read the "
"Docs project with any Git provider using :term:`webhooks <webhook>`. Manual "
"integration is most useful for Git providers that we don't support with "
"automatic configuration. Automatic configuration is supported for |"
"git_providers_and|."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:9
msgid ""
"Git repositories that are imported manually **do not** have the required "
"setup to send back a **commit status**. If you need this integration, you "
"have to :doc:`configure the repository automatically </reference/git-"
"integration>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:30
msgid "Manual integration setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:32
msgid ""
"You need to configure your Git provider integration to call a webhook that "
"alerts Read the Docs of changes. Read the Docs will sync versions and build "
"your documentation whenever a Git commit happens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:37
msgid "GitHub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:39
msgid ""
"Go to :menuselection:`Settings --> Webhooks` of your **GitHub repository**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:40
#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:69
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Add webhook`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:41
msgid ""
"For **Payload URL**, use the URL of the integration on your **Read the Docs "
"project**, found on your project's :menuselection:`Settings --> "
"Integrations` page. You may need to prepend *https://* to the URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:44
#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:99
msgid ""
"For **Content type**, both *application/json* and *application/x-www-form-"
"urlencoded* work"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:46
#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:73
#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:101
msgid ""
"Fill the **Secret** field with the value from the integration on Read the "
"Docs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:47
msgid ""
"Select **Let me select individual events**, and mark **Branch or tag "
"creation**, **Branch or tag deletion**, **Pull requests** and **Pushes** "
"events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:49
#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:104
msgid "Ensure **Active** is enabled; it is by default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:50
msgid ""
"Finish by clicking :guilabel:`Add webhook`.  You may be prompted to enter "
"your GitHub password to confirm your action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:52
msgid ""
"You can verify if the webhook is working at the bottom of the GitHub page "
"under **Recent Deliveries**. If you see a Response 200, then the webhook is "
"correctly configured. For a 403 error, it's likely that the Payload URL is "
"incorrect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:56
msgid "GitLab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:58
msgid ""
"Go to :menuselection:`Settings --> Webhooks` of your **GitLab repository**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:59
msgid ""
"For **URL**, use the URL of the integration on **Read the Docs project**, "
"found on your project's :menuselection:`Settings --> Integrations` page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:61
msgid ""
"Fill the **Secret token** field with the value from the integration on Read "
"the Docs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:62
msgid ""
"Leave the default **Push events** selected, additionally mark **Tag push "
"events** and **Merge request events**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:64
#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:105
msgid "Finish by clicking :guilabel:`Add Webhook`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:66
msgid "Bitbucket"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:68
msgid ""
"Go to :menuselection:`Settings --> Webhooks` of your **Bitbucket repository**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:70
#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:96
msgid ""
"For **URL**, use the URL of the integration on Read the Docs, found on your "
"project's :menuselection:`Settings --> Integrations` page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:72
msgid "Under **Triggers**, **Repository push** should be selected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:74
msgid "Finish by clicking :guilabel:`Save`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:76
msgid "Gitea"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:78
msgid "These instructions apply to any Gitea instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:82
msgid ""
"This isn't officially supported, but using the \"GitHub webhook\" is an "
"effective workaround, because Gitea uses the same payload as GitHub. The "
"generic webhook is not compatible with Gitea. See `issue #8364`_ for more "
"details. Official support may be implemented in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:86
msgid "On Read the Docs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:88
msgid ""
"Manually create a \"GitHub webhook\" integration (this will show a warning "
"about the webhook not being correctly set up, that will go away when the "
"webhook is configured in Gitea)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:92
msgid "On your Gitea instance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:94
msgid ""
"Go to :menuselection:`Settings --> Webhooks` of your **Gitea repository**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:95
msgid "Create a new webhook of type \"Gitea\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:98
msgid "Leave the default **HTTP Method** as POST"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:102
msgid ""
"Select **Choose events**, and mark **Branch or tag creation**, **Branch or "
"tag deletion** and **Push** events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:106
msgid "Test the webhook with :guilabel:`Delivery test`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:108
msgid ""
"Finally, on Read the Docs, check that the warnings have disappeared and the "
"delivery test triggered a build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:113
msgid "Others"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:115
msgid ""
"Other providers are supported through a generic webhook, see :ref:`webhook-"
"integration-generic`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:118
msgid "Payload validation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:120
msgid ""
"All integrations are created with a secret token, this offers a way to "
"verify that a webhook request is legitimate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:123
msgid "This validation is done according to each provider:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:125
msgid "`GitHub <https://developer.github.com/webhooks/securing/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:126
msgid ""
"`GitLab <https://docs.gitlab.com/ee/user/project/integrations/"
"webhooks.html#validate-payloads-by-using-a-secret-token>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:127
msgid ""
"`Bitbucket <https://support.atlassian.com/bitbucket-cloud/docs/manage-"
"webhooks/#Secure-webhooks>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:131
msgid "Managing Integrations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:133
msgid ""
"To manually set up an integration, go to your "
"project's :menuselection:`Settings --> Integrations`, click "
"on :guilabel:`Add integration`, and select the integration type you'd like "
"to add."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:136
msgid ""
"As an example, the URL pattern looks like this: ``https://"
"app.readthedocs.org/api/v2/webhook/<project-name>/<id>/*``. Use this URL "
"when setting up a new integration with your provider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:142
msgid "Using the generic API integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:144
msgid ""
"For repositories that are not hosted with a supported provider, we also "
"offer a generic API endpoint for triggering project builds. Similar to "
"webhook integrations, this integration has a specific URL, which can be "
"found on the project's **Integrations** dashboard page "
"(:menuselection:`Settings --> Integrations`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:149
msgid ""
"Token authentication is required to use the generic endpoint, you will find "
"this token on the integration details page. The token should be passed in as "
"a request parameter, either as form data or as part of JSON data input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:154
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:156
msgid "This endpoint accepts the following arguments during an HTTP POST:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:158
msgid "branches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:159
msgid ""
"The names of the branches to trigger builds for. This can either be an array "
"of branch name strings, or just a single branch name string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:162
msgid "Default: **latest**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:164
msgid "token"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:165
msgid ""
"The integration token found on the project's **Integrations** dashboard page "
"(:menuselection:`Settings --> Integrations`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:169
msgid "default_branch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:170
msgid ""
"This is the default branch of the repository (ie. the one checked out when "
"cloning the repository without arguments)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:173
msgid "*Optional*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:175
msgid ""
"For example, to build the ``dev`` branch of project ``example-project`` "
"using the integration token ``1234``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:180
msgid ""
"$ curl \\\n"
"    --data \"branches=dev&token=1234&default_branch=main\" \\\n"
"    https://app.readthedocs.org/api/v2/webhook/example-project/1/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:186
msgid ""
"import requests\n"
"\n"
"URL = \"https://app.readthedocs.org/api/v2/webhook/example-project/1/\"\n"
"TOKEN = \"1234\"\n"
"response = requests.post(\n"
"    URL,\n"
"    data={\"branches\": \"dev\", \"token\": TOKEN, \"default_branch\": "
"\"main\"},\n"
")\n"
"print(response.json())"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:198
msgid ""
"A command like the one above could be called from a cron job or from a `Git "
"hook`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:203
msgid "Authentication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:205
msgid ""
"This endpoint requires authentication. If authenticating with an integration "
"token, a check will determine if the token is valid and matches the given "
"project. If instead an authenticated user is used to make this request, a "
"check will be performed to ensure the authenticated user is an owner of the "
"project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:211
msgid "Troubleshooting Git provider webhooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:214
msgid "Debugging webhooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:216
msgid ""
"If you are experiencing problems with an existing webhook, you may be able "
"to use the integration detail page to help debug the issue. Each project "
"integration, such as a webhook or the generic API endpoint, stores the HTTP "
"exchange that takes place between Read the Docs and the external source. "
"You'll find a list of these exchanges in any of the integration detail pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:223
msgid "Webhook activation failed. Make sure you have the necessary permissions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:225
msgid ""
"If you find this error, make sure your user has permissions over the "
"repository. In case of GitHub, check that you have granted access to the "
"Read the Docs `OAuth App`_ to your organization. A similar workflow is "
"required for other supported providers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:235
msgid "My project isn't automatically building"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/setup/git-repo-manual.rst:237
msgid ""
"If your project isn't automatically building, you can check your integration "
"on Read the Docs to see the payload sent to our servers. If there is no "
"recent activity on your Read the Docs project webhook integration, then it's "
"likely that your Git provider is not configured correctly. If there is "
"payload information on your Read the Docs project, you might need to verify "
"that your versions are configured to build correctly."
msgstr ""
